{"name":"Vintage Chartreuse","hex":"#a3b22e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vintage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The yield of grapes or wine from a vineyard or district during one season.","Wine, especially high-quality, identified as to year and vineyard or district of origin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a vintage, or to wine identified by a specific vintage.","Having an enduring appeal; high-quality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vintage"},{"term":"chartreuse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellow or green liqueur made by Carthusian monks.","A greenish-yellow color."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright yellowish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chartreuse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vintage","blocks":[{"text":"In winemaking, vintage is the process of picking grapes to create wine. A vintage wine is one made from grapes that were all, or primarily, grown and harvested in a single specified year. In certain wines, it can denote quality, as in Port wine, where Port houses make and declare vintage Port in their best years. From this tradition, a common, though not strictly correct, usage applies the term to any wine that is perceived to be particularly old or of a particularly high quality."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cup_vintage_Cdm_Paris_320_n1.jpg/330px-Cup_vintage_Cdm_Paris_320_n1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vintage"},{"title":"Chartreuse (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green also referred to as yellow-green or greenish yellow. It was named because of its resemblance to the French liqueur green chartreuse, introduced in 1764. Similarly, chartreuse yellow is a yellow color mixed with a small amount of green, named after the drink yellow chartreuse. The wavelength and frequency of chartreuse is near 547.5 nm or 547.5 THz."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/RAF-Cardington-Shed02_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-RAF-Cardington-Shed02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chartreuse_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png/500px-The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png/1280px-The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png/500px-The_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Vintagers, after a miniature of the \"Dialogues de Saint Gregoire\" (13th century)—manuscript of the Royal Library of Belgium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Vintagers_after_a_Miniature_of_the_Dialogues_de_Saint_Gregoire_Thirteenth_Century_Manuscript_of_the_Royal_Library_of_Brussels.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Jacob_Philipp_Hackert_00